`opentelemetry-sdk`: Add a private `MetricReader._allows_async_instrument`
hook that gates whether an asynchronous instrument's callback runs during a
reader's collection. The capability is checked before the callback executes and
again before each of its measurements is stored, so a reader without the
required capability never triggers restricted callbacks and cannot cache their
results. The default implementation allows every asynchronous instrument,
preserving existing reader behavior.
